From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] os_install_service: let the user pick the install disk

The service chose the install disk by itself (largest non-removable
disk that is not the installer). NickelOS shows a disk picker when more
than one disk qualifies:

- GetInstallDestinations returns the candidate disks as JSON, best
  first, with path, model, size, removable and which one an automatic
  install would choose (lsblk now also reports MODEL).
- StartOsInstallTo(device_path) installs to the chosen disk; it refuses
  any path that is not a current candidate.

zram devices are never candidates: lsblk's `--exclude 253` missed zram
when its major number differed, so the automatic choice could pick it.

StartOsInstall (automatic choice) and auto-install are unchanged otherwise.

---
